# dims.json and masks.json are build products of avian/scripts/build_masks.py,
# derived entirely from whatever PNGs are in avian/assets/illustrations/. Both
# this fork and upstream regenerate them whenever illustrations change, so a
# textual merge of the two is meaningless - the correct resolution is always
# "rebuild from the merged set of illustrations".
#
# merge=ours keeps our copy during a merge instead of raising a conflict. That
# is not the final answer, it just avoids a pointless conflict: after merging
# upstream, run
#
#     python3 avian/scripts/build_masks.py
#
# which picks up any illustrations the merge brought in and rewrites both files
# correctly. Committing that rebuild is the real resolution.
#
# The "ours" driver has to be enabled once per clone (it is a config setting,
# not something .gitattributes can carry):
#
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
#
# Without it git falls back to a normal merge and you get the conflict you
# would have got anyway - so a clone that forgets this is no worse off.
avian/frontend/dims.json   merge=ours
avian/frontend/masks.json  merge=ours

# Keep illustrations out of textual diffs entirely.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
